The retried messages all have `order_created >= 469`, which matches the first anomaly timestamp exactly. Orders created before t=469 (including those after the sync-job deploy at t=410) are not affected. This rules out the sync-job deploy as the cause. The invoice_text samples from E13 look structurally normal, so I need to check whether orders created around t=469 have a different layout compared to baseline orders.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT id, invoice_text FROM orders WHERE order_id IN ('ORD-00907','ORD-00911','ORD-00920') OR id IN ('ORD-00907','ORD-00911','ORD-00920')",
      "why": "Inspect the actual invoice_text of the failing orders to identify what layout change appeared at t=469 that differs from the baseline samples in E13."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "invoice-agent",
      "kind": "bad_input",
      "mechanism": "Invoices arriving from suppliers starting at t=469 have an unexpected layout that invoice-agent cannot parse, causing extraction failures and repeated retries until the retry budget is exhausted.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E3", "E4", "E14"],
      "refuting": ["E6"],
      "explains": ["I6_retry_budget"],
      "repair_plan": []
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All retried messages belong to orders created at t>=469, consistent with a new invoice layout arriving from suppliers at that time; the sync-job deploy at t=410 is a decoy as no messages from the t=410–469 window are affected."
}
```
